From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fit the engine to a phone with 512 MB that jetsams at 282 MB

The engine believed it was always out of memory; the memory bands are now
calibrated against the jetsam limit, the two cheap caches stay while the heavy
ones go, canvases are capped in total again, layer memory ceilings are sized
for this screen rather than a 3x phone, and text and glyph caches are sized for
it. A timer that fires every ten seconds no longer calls os_log, and the web
thread can opt in to a real-time scheduling policy.
